    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29804" root="عق" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآءٌ عُقٌّ</span></b> , with damm, (K, TA,) or ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَقٌّ</span></b> , (thus
written in my copies of the S and in the O,) and
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُقَاقٌ</span></b> , (O, K, TA,) <i>Bitter water:</i> (S, O, K:)
or <i>intensely bitter water:</i> used alike as sing. and
pl.: (TA:) like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُعٌّ</span>, (TA,) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قَعٌّ</span>, (S, O,) and
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">قُعَاعٌ</span>. (O, TA.)

